--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
The darkness folds back like cloth. Three cards hover before you, edges glowing faintly. The first turns: **The High Priestess**, moon-crowned, seated between twin pillars. A hush enters your chest, as if someone just whispered your name from behind a curtain.

The second card flips: **Six of Cups**, two children trading flowers in a sunlit yard. Your mouth tastes of old summer water from a garden hose. The third card turns: **Knight of Pentacles**, a figure on a heavy horse holding a single gold coin. Your palms feel the weight of soil under fingernails.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The void thins. Cold stone presses against your back. You lie on the floor of the ruined observatory west of Virell, dawn light leaking through the broken dome. A jackdaw perches on a cracked astrolabe, watching you wake.

