--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
The morning light through the cracked shutter is a dull gold stripe across your cot. You wake in the attic room of the Broken Lantern Inn, Elaris Hollow, tasting smoke from last night’s hearth on your tongue. A clay cup waits on the bedside plank; when you reach for it, the cup skids an inch, stops, and is simply pottery again. You stare, throat dry, unsure if the cot creaked or the world did.

Boots thud downstairs and the market wakes outside. A dog barks, metal clinks, someone laughs. You pull on your coat, open the warped shutter, and see Old Well Square below. A short man in a patched trader’s vest paces by the mossy stones, wringing a wool cap. He spots you, relief flickering across his face.

“You there—sorry—could you spare a moment?” He gestures toward the forest edge. “Raiders scattered my stock last night. They dropped my sample box near the Whispering trees. Nothing fierce, just… could you fetch it? I’ll stand you breakfast.” His eyes keep darting to the treeline, as though the box might wander off if no one hurries.

