--- MODEL OUTPUT ---
The cracked flagstones of Old Well Square warm under the morning sun. A gaunt merchant in a patched wool coat paces beside the mossy rim of the well, muttering under his breath. When he spots you, relief floods his face.

"Please—wait." He steps closer, hands trembling. "Last night someone broke the straps on my cart. They took most goods, but a small iron lockbox rolled into the Whispering Forest Edge. My trade samples are inside. Nothing grand, just spice jars and silk scraps, yet without them I can't buy tomorrow's bread."

He glances toward the treeline visible beyond the square's low wall. "I would go myself, but my knees shake just looking at those shadows. If you could walk the path and bring the box back, I'd share what little coin I have left."

The square is quiet except for the creak of his empty cart. Sparrows hop between cobbles, hunting crumbs.

